\f1\fs20 BROWNING, Mont. (AP) _ A ``Flying Elvis\uc0\u8243  suffered a broken pelvis during the grand opening of the Glacier Peaks Casino here. Paul Moran is a member of The Flying Elvi, a 10-member skydiving team made up of Elvis Presley impersonators, who were hired to parachute into the parking lot at the casino Friday.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Other members of the troupe said the Las Vegas man apparently misjudged the landing and hit the ground at 50 mph.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>``I talked to his family (Monday) and they said he is doing well, but he did break his pelvis,\uc0\u8243  said Gary Green, casino manager.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Moran was taken to the Blackfeet Community Hospital and then flown to Harborview Medical Center in Seattle, where he is listed in serious condition in the intensive care unit.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>An Elvis impersonator suffered a smashed pelvis during a parachute jump that went wrong.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Flying Elvis - aka Paul Moran - found himself All Shook Up after he hit the ground in a Montana car park at up to 50mph.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>His injuries, however, could have been far more serious were it not for his rubber wig, which cushioned the blow he suffered to his head.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Mr Moran was part of a 10-man team of Elvis impersonators taking part in the jump to promote the opening of a casino in Browning. He is recovering in hospital.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
